# --- Folders to ignore (Bloat & Caches) ---
# Most apps store temporary data or heavy caches in these subfolders
**/cache/
**/Cache/
**/cached/
**/logs/
**/temp/
**/tmp/

# --- Specific App Bloat ---
# Browsers (heavy and contain personal history/cookies)
google-chrome/
microsoft-edge/
BraveSoftware/
mozilla/

# Discord & Electron apps
discord/Cache/
discord/Code\ Cache/
discord/GPUCache/

# IDE Caches (VS Code, JetBrains)
Code/CachedData/
Code/User/History/
Code/User/workspaceStorage/
Code/Backups/

# --- System & Environment ---
# Python & Node environment noise
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/venv/
**/.env
**/.direnv/

# Nix specific (if you use flakes or direnv)
result
result-*

# --- Security & Sensitive Data ---
# Never track your SSH keys or GPG keys if they happen to be linked here
**/ssh/
**/gnupg/
# Ignore credentials/token files
**/*token*
**/*history*
**/.python_history
**/zsh_history

# --- Media & Thumbnails ---
**/thumbnails/
**/Thumbnails/

# VS Code / Antigravity Bloat
Antigravity/
Code/
# System/App specific bloat
evolution/
dconf/
ibus/
# Large binary icons/images
wlogout/icons/*.png
# General cache ignore
**/CachedData/
**/Code Cache/
**/CachedExtensionVSIXs/
# Ignore system state and database files
*.db
*.settings-ported
gnome-initial-setup-done
mimeapps.list
user-dirs.*
pulse/
simple-scan/
